## 4-agent team (one repo, one session at a time)
| Chat name | Role rule | May write | Never |
|---|---|---|---|
| QE Planner | `qe-planner.mdc` | `docs/agents/**` (plans, STATUS, decisions), `docs/audits/**` | app code, git writes, migrations, DB |
| QE Coder | `qe-coder.mdc` | app code + new migrations per the approved prompt; coding report, BASELINES, api-catalog, STATUS | anything outside the prompt |
| QE Auditor | `qe-auditor.mdc` | `docs/agents/reports/audit/**`, STATUS | code, git writes, migrations, DB |
| QE Tester | `qe-tester.mdc` | `docs/agents/reports/testing/**`, `docs/agents/tests/**`, STATUS | code, git writes, migrations, committed DB writes |

- **Flow:** Planner (plan, then Amit approves) → Coder (verify → migrate → commit → push) → Auditor → Tester → Planner (Hinglish summary to Amit) → next plan.
- **Handoff:** Chats can't call each other. Each agent:
  1. writes its report file
  2. updates `docs/agents/STATUS.md` (stage, owner, next action, IST time from `date '+%Y-%m-%d %H:%M %Z'`)
  3. ends its reply with one `NEXT:` line that Amit pastes into the next chat
- **Session ids:** S6…S10, F1…, B0…, D1…. Bug-fix rounds are `<ID>a`, then `<ID>c`, and so on. `S6b` is reserved for the follow-up in decision #7.
- **Files:**
  - `docs/agents/plans/<ID>_plan.md` and `<ID>_coder_prompt.md`
  - `docs/agents/reports/coding/<ID>_coding.md`, `reports/audit/<ID>_audit.md`, `reports/testing/<ID>_testing.md`
- With no role rule attached and no role named, behave as a normal assistant under `00-project-core`. Don't pick a role yourself.
- A role rule's limits override any general instruction in the chat. If Amit asks a role for something outside its limits, say which chat should do it.
- Rule files (`.cursor/rules/`, `.cursorrules`): the Planner proposes a change first. The Planner edits those files when Amit says to update the rules.
